<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ēlysĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἠλύσιον</span>, the abode of the blest, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Elysium</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 5,
				735</span></i> Serv.; 6, 542; 744 al.; cf. Heyne <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				6, 675 sq.</span></i>; and ejusd. libri Exc. VIII. p. 1019
			Wagn.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ēlysĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Elysian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 38</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tib. 1, 3, 58</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
			175</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					10, 101</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plagae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 6,
					58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 111</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
					12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chaos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 520</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rosae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 7, 60: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puella,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Proserpine</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					10, 24</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Elysii</span></b> , ōrum, m. (sc.
			campi), <i>the Elysian Fields</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 9,
			52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 6, 699</span></i>.</div>
